{
  "sn55.24:0.1": "Linked Discourses 55.24 ",
  "sn55.24:0.2": "3. About Sarakāni ",
  "sn55.24:0.3": "About Sarakāni (1st) ",
  "sn55.24:1.1": "At Kapilavatthu. ",
  "sn55.24:1.2": "Now at that time Sarakāni the Sakyan had passed away. ",
  "sn55.24:1.3": "The Buddha declared that he was ",
  "sn55.24:1.4": "a stream-enterer, not liable to be reborn in the underworld, assured, destined for awakening. ",
  "sn55.24:1.5": "At that, several Sakyans came together complaining, grumbling, and objecting, ",
  "sn55.24:1.6": "“Oh lord, how incredible, how amazing! ",
  "sn55.24:1.7": "Who can’t become a stream-enterer these days? ",
  "sn55.24:1.8": "For the Buddha even declared Sarakāni to be a stream-enterer after he passed away. ",
  "sn55.24:1.9": "",
  "sn55.24:1.10": "",
  "sn55.24:1.11": "Sarakāni was too weak for the training; he used to drink liquor.” ",
  "sn55.24:2.1": "Then Mahānāma the Sakyan went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and told him what had happened. The Buddha said: ",
  "sn55.24:2.2": "",
  "sn55.24:2.3": "",
  "sn55.24:2.4": "",
  "sn55.24:2.5": "",
  "sn55.24:2.6": "",
  "sn55.24:2.7": "",
  "sn55.24:2.8": "",
  "sn55.24:2.9": "",
  "sn55.24:2.10": "",
  "sn55.24:2.11": "",
  "sn55.24:3.1": "“Mahānāma, when a lay follower has for a long time gone for refuge to the Buddha, the teaching, and the Saṅgha, how could they go to the underworld? ",
  "sn55.24:3.2": "And if anyone should rightly be said to ",
  "sn55.24:3.3": "have for a long time gone for refuge to